  "guide_title": "Usage Guide: Get the most out of it",
  "guide_step1_title": "1. Quick Selection & Loading",
  "guide_step1_desc": "Select your Origin directory and one or more Destination directories. You can also drag and drop folders directly into the loading zones for an instant start.",
  "guide_step2_title": "2. Explore the Status Matrix",
  "guide_step2_desc": "Once processed, the matrix will show you the status of each file using semantic colors: Green (identical), Yellow (differs in size or content) and Red/Grey (missing).",
  "guide_step3_title": "3. View & Navigate the Diff",
  "guide_step3_desc": "Click on any row to open the side-by-side differences view. Use the arrow buttons at the top to safely jump from one difference to another without manual scrolling.",
  "guide_step4_title": "4. Clean Noise with Normalizers",
  "guide_step4_desc": "Go to the Filters tab to ignore whitespaces, comments or normalize JSON/YAML/XML structures. This allows you to compare only the useful content, discarding format differences.",
  "guide_step5_title": "5. Control with the Terminal",
  "guide_step5_desc": "Use the integrated command terminal to speed up your workflow. Open the console at the bottom and run /sync to compare, /cls to clear slots, or /theme to toggle visual themes.",
  "guide_step6_title": "6. Check the History",
  "guide_step6_desc": "Your comparison profiles and previous matrices are securely saved in your local database (IndexedDB) so you can consult and re-scan them in your next session.",
